BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260707T040624Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53188682710853
DTSTART:20260825T213000Z
DTEND:20260825T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Gregg Museum of Art & Design to learn about the specia
 l exhibition Crafting Sanctuaries: Black Spaces of the Great Depression So
 uth with the curator Tamir Williams. Crafting Sanctuaries expands the popu
 lar visual memory of the Great Depression by highlighting rarely seen Farm
  Security Administration images of rural Black southerners and their spati
 al worlds during the 1930s and 1940s. Williams will share a short overview
  of the exhibition. A conversation with NC State faculty members Ajamu Dil
 lahunt-Holloway\, an assistant professor of African American history and p
 ublic history\, and Nishani Frazier\, a professor of history and director 
 of public history\, and North Carolina Poet Laureate Jaki Shelton Green wi
 ll follow the overview.\n\nThe exhibition will be on display at the Gregg 
 from Aug. 6\, 2026\, to  Jan. 16\, 2027.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design\, Main Lobby
SUMMARY:Reflections on Crafting Sanctuaries 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/reflections-on-crafting-sanct
 uaries
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
CATEGORIES:Information Session
END:VEVENT
